# Copy to .env.local for development, or paste into Coolify's environment tab
# for the droplet. Nothing here is required for the site to build and run: every
# value has a working default or a documented fallback, which is deliberate,
# because a portfolio that cannot be cloned and started in one command is a
# portfolio nobody runs.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy target. Set by the build scripts, not by hand.
#   unset       Vercel, or `next dev`
#   standalone  Docker, set by `npm run build:standalone`
#   export      static HTML, set by `npm run build:static`
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_OUTPUT=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The hostname Traefik routes to on the droplet. Used by
# deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml only.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SITE_HOST=balisa.dev

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uptime Kuma, once the droplet is up. Without this the infra page reports
# reachability and response time measured at render, and says so. With it, the
# page can report real uptime history.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UPTIME_KUMA_URL=https://status.balisa.dev

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared Postgres on the droplet. Required by
# deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml, not by this site.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# POSTGRES_USER=app
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_DB=app

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Lifts the GitHub API rate limit for the star counts. The site works
# without it and falls back to the committed numbers.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
